cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AO Commons Knowledge Graph"
message: >-
  If you use this corpus, please cite it. Cite a release rather than the
  repository where you can: releases are checksummed and keep their mistakes,
  so a citation to one means the same thing next year.
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "AO Commons"
    website: "https://aocommons.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AO-Commons/knowledge-graph"
url: "https://ao-commons.github.io/knowledge-graph/"
abstract: >-
  A maintained map of research on autonomous organizations: organizations in
  which machine agents hold operational or decision authority. The unit is the
  claim rather than the paper - one thing a paper asserts, stored with the
  exact sentence it was drawn from, what kind of claim it is, and whose result
  it is. 363 records and 349 claims read from 27 papers, under a
  purpose-built taxonomy of 103 topics. Every release also ships as a MIRA graph.
keywords:
  - autonomous organizations
  - multi-agent systems
  - AI agents
  - knowledge graph
  - research corpus
  - taxonomy
  - AI governance
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
date-released: "2026-11-03"
version: "v0.12.0"
